{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342587-diablerising-a-strix","id":1342587,"title":"Diablerising a strix","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-20T15:40:37-07:00","id":1342587,"title":"Diablerising a strix","content":"T was wondering what would happen if a vampire commit amaranth at a a vampire possesed by a strix?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25728-marios_tzi","name":"Marios_Tzi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T16:38:06-07:00","id":1342602,"title":"","content":"My inner rule lawyer isn\u2019t sure but the fact that when they leave a host that host gets the benefit of any act of diablerie and also needs to make the braking point roll implies that Strix are not simply concentrated vampiric essence.<br /> It\u2019s also interesting that a Strix always gains only one Shadow Potency from the act regardless of their victims SP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4714,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","user":"Live Bait","date":". 10-20-2019, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T06:19:33-07:00","id":1342703,"title":"","content":"If I'm STing in this purely hypothetical and unlikely scenario, the Strix essence is automatically and inescapably trapped in the diablerist and I would roll a 50/50 percentile to see if the diablerist manages to pull the &quot;soul&quot; of the host vampire also or if it escapes. <br /> The diablerist gets the standard diablerie prize as if he had diablerized the vampire unpossessed but detects as permanently tainted (by the Strix essence) and no amount of Aggravated damage clears it.<br /> It's an inverted possession, the diablerist can spend a willpower point to force the Strix use it's relevant abilities for the diablerist to use if it can pay relevant activation costs but the diablerist has to keep the Strix &quot;fed&quot; as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T07:10:40-07:00","id":1342707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342587-diablerising-a-strix?p=1342703#post1342703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm STing in this purely hypothetical and unlikely scenario, the Strix essence is automatically and inescapably trapped in the diablerist and I would roll a 50/50 percentile to see if the diablerist manages to pull the &amp;quot;soul&amp;quot; of the host vampire also or if it escapes. <br /> The diablerist gets the standard diablerie prize as if he had diablerized the vampire unpossessed but detects as permanently tainted (by the Strix essence) and no amount of Aggravated damage clears it.<br /> It's an inverted possession, the diablerist can spend a willpower point to force the Strix use it's relevant abilities for the diablerist to use if it can pay relevant activation costs but the diablerist has to keep the Strix &amp;quot;fed&amp;quot; as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think you'd feed it with vitae or with vice? I feel like this could be a really cool opportunity to implement a shadow guide (from wraith).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T08:43:05-07:00","id":1342717,"title":"","content":"This is so rare that whatever happens needs to be <i>spectacular</i>. I'm thinking something like permanent yellow eyes, the vampire's blood turning to smoke, and memories of the ancient past, before writing or language or fire, when human beings were merely instincts and fear and wits and hunger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T09:11:44-07:00","id":1342719,"title":"","content":"We've always had attempted diablerie on a Strix be an invitation to being possessed (even if the Strix doesn't have the right Embodiment). If the Strix fails to possess the diablerist, it's likely ejected rather than diablerised (its former host is diablerised either way, unless it was a human or a corpse). We're drawing from the story of En Isiratuu in Ancient Mysteries who was tricked into attempting to diablerise a being containing seven &quot;shadowy demons&quot; and failed spectacularly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T09:21:33-07:00","id":1342723,"title":"","content":"Golconda.<br /> <br /> I'm only halfway joking - but you'd be a human-derivative and you've eaten a human spirit-derivative. In a sense, you'd be the most complete person alive. I'm not sure how I would make it awesome enough a PC, but I'd probably make it terrible and horrible and tragic for an NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T09:43:39-07:00","id":1342729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342587-diablerising-a-strix?p=1342707#post1342707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think you'd feed it with vitae or with vice? I feel like this could be a really cool opportunity to implement a shadow guide (from wraith).</div> </div> </div> </div>Both. As time passes, vitae alone wouldn't be enough to sustain the Strix. The diablerist is going to have to go out and purchase relevant merits to accumulate willpower from indulging vices but he doesn't get the willpower, the Strix essence does. I'd also implement mechanics of some sort where the Strix eats away at the diablerist's Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T12:39:34-07:00","id":1342777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342587-diablerising-a-strix?p=1342729#post1342729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both. As time passes, vitae alone wouldn't be enough to sustain the Strix. The diablerist is going to have to go out and purchase relevant merits to accumulate willpower from indulging vices but he doesn't get the willpower, the Strix essence does. I'd also implement mechanics of some sort where the Strix eats away at the diablerist's Humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that that's necessary. I seem to remember something about the Strix getting WP just by observing someone else committing the Strix's vice.<br /> <br /> There are probably two ways I'd do it.<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>You've got a Strix in your head.</b></li> </ol><br /> I think in the back of the core book there was a twist called something like Beast Guides - where your beast offers you willpower in exchange for actions (but isn't necessarily bound to give you the WP). Maybe rather than frenzy, you have to deal with the Strix taking over. It offers its powers at the cost of WP, and offers WP/advice/etc for indulging its Vice. Whenever you would normally resist frenzy, you instead resist possession. And the Strix can initiate a frenzy roll whenever it wants. <br /> <br /> I would worry about this being too adversarial between ST and player, so I would set it up with a player as the Strix.<br /> <br /> <b> 2. You're becoming like the Strix</b><br /> Or alternately, you gain the Vice, and maybe your frenzies change in nature. They're more dissociative. You don't black/red-out. Instead, you just go cold. Instead of running a way during fear frenzy because of injury, instead you just start playing with the injury or hurting yourself again. You get the Vice. You can spend WP to use Dread Powers. As you lose Humanity you get more of those memories Rose mentioned, more access to the dread powers and banes.<br /> <br /> One thing that gets ignored a lot is the Strix's role as a harbinger/omen of catastrophe. Maybe there's a way to work it in too. Maybe bad shit happens around you, or you get a sense for coming catastrophe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","user":"DubiousRuffian","date":". 10-21-2019, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T08:45:04-07:00","id":1342951,"title":"","content":"In my game I have an important and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fintan_mac_B%C3%B3chra\" target=\"_blank\">extremely old NPC</a> who in various episodes has been shown as a shadow-dwelling vampiric sorceror and in the past as a kind of smokey shadow-wolf spirit with two pairs of yellow eyes and two pairs of wings. In my head, he consumed one (or two) strix and was subsequently physically destroyed--but escaped to ephemeral form.<br /> <br /> How this could happen remains to be revealed but my handwave includes sorcery of course... and clearly this is a character in unique circumstances. It's also possible that he actually is a strix in synthesis with the vampire. Regardless, in practice he exemplifies the vice of the strix in question: sloth. The character does a lot less than he could, and mostly advises and teaches and watches, while prodding others to take measures against his ancient enemy.<br /> <br /> In general, any situation that results in a fusion of strix and vampire (or strix and human) that doesn't leave the strix in command should emphasize the vice and how it assumes greater influence. I like the idea that during &quot;frenzy&quot; a character becomes manifestly more strix-like and accesses dread powers otherwise not available. But: there should also be ways for the fusion to increase the power of the strix; as others allude to, there is a kind of completeness that synthesis could give strix that they lack by themselves. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T12:28:45-07:00","id":1342997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342587-diablerising-a-strix?p=1342951#post1342951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my game I have an important and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fintan_mac_B%C3%B3chra\" target=\"_blank\">extremely old NPC</a> , there is a kind of completeness that synthesis could give strix that they lack by themselves.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, they get a body. They lost the connection to their bodies when they split off, and now they're pissed because they lack bodies. That's part of why they possess people.<br /> <br /> Someone above mentioned giving a roll to see if the Strix takes over after diablerie. I'd probably only give that roll to an NPC (unless the player was actually cool with losing their PC), and the NPC lost that roll, I'd probably say that the Strix takes over, but now is actually capable of experiencing kindness and togetherness. They can actually get rehabilitated.<br /> <br /> But assuming the vampire stays in control... how would they be made &quot;complete&quot;? That line of Kierkegaard's about how &quot;we can only understand life backwards, but must live it forward&quot; comes to mind. Maybe the vampire gains some kind of connection to fate, similar to the dhampyr? Or, just going by association with Kierkegaard, K thinks we experience anxiety because we have free will and don't know if we'll choose to sin. Maybe a &quot;whole&quot; vampire no longer detaches due to malevolent acts. Or they straight up do not frenzy..<br /> <br /> Idk, I'm just spitballing.<br /> <br /> Also, Fintan looks really interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","user":"DubiousRuffian","date":". 10-22-2019, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T19:39:31-08:00","id":1348116,"title":"","content":"The Strix should have never been introduced.<br /> <br /> They are practically vampires, themselves. Then there's the meta-fiction of a curious Strix possessing a corpse.<br /> <br /> Boom, vampire origin. The whole thing from VtM you tried to avoid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T03:24:18-08:00","id":1348200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DubiousRuffian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342587-diablerising-a-strix?p=1342997#post1342997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone above mentioned giving a roll to see if the Strix takes over after diablerie. I'd probably only give that roll to an NPC (unless the player was actually cool with losing their PC), and the NPC lost that roll, I'd probably say that the Strix takes over, but now is actually capable of experiencing kindness and togetherness. They can actually get rehabilitated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just make sure the players are aware of the risk and/or make sure it's reversible. I.e. the particular Strix that the PC attempted to diablerise is more than happy to make a deal with the other PCs for releasing their new puppet.<br /> I don't really see the point of messing with the Strix mentally, though. It's pretty on point for Strix to just screw Kindred over even in unexpected ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342587-diablerising-a-strix?p=1348116#post1348116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Strix should have never been introduced.<br /> <br /> They are practically vampires, themselves. Then there's the meta-fiction of a curious Strix possessing a corpse.<br /> <br /> Boom, vampire origin. The whole thing from VtM you tried to avoid.</div> </div> </div> </div>For someone who argued there's no canon in VtR, you're awfully quick assuming a single, definite origin for vampires based on circumstantial evidence despite there being multiple optional origins for each Clan. If you don't want the Strix to be the origin of all vampires, don't have them be the origin for all vampires. Doing so doesn't invalidate the Strix or go against the text in any way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T11:41:42-08:00","id":1348312,"title":"","content":"Hell, there's no canon in Requiem on whether vampires even have a single origin or not. It's possible that all vampires were once one species that diverged. It's also possible that all vampires were originally totally different types of creatures which converged on the form of &quot;looks like a human, sustains itself on the life-force in blood&quot;. A couple different 1e books explored the latter option.<br /> <br /> The Strix may <i>claim</i> they created vampires, but anything a Strix says should be taken with many grains of salt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T09:39:23-08:00","id":1348494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342587-diablerising-a-strix?p=1348312#post1348312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">anything a Strix says should be taken with many grains of salt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically, said grains of salt should be hurled into its eyes and then left on the ground for it to count.<br /> <br /> While you run away as quickly as possible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T06:35:22-08:00","id":1348658,"title":"","content":"@<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro\">Illuminostro - </a></b>They are a type of vampire.<br /> <br /> Personally, I love the Strix, but if they aren't for you, don't have them in your game. In the four books that have been published in 2e, I'm pretty sure they've only shown up in the corebook, and mostly in a single chapter. They aren't central enough to the game to have trouble cutting them out.<br /> <br /> Edit: Just remembered, there's passing mention of a yellow-eyed thing in the Korea section of Guide to the Night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24634,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","user":"DubiousRuffian","date":". 11-15-2019, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24634-dubiousruffian","name":"DubiousRuffian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"210"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T09:33:51-08:00","id":1350653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342587-diablerising-a-strix?p=1348116#post1348116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Strix should have never been introduced.<br /> <br /> They are practically vampires, themselves. Then there's the meta-fiction of a curious Strix possessing a corpse.<br /> <br /> Boom, vampire origin. The whole thing from VtM you tried to avoid.</div> </div> </div> </div>What\u2019s so curious about this is that there\u2019s been, what, three more supplements for VtR 2e so far? I can\u2019t even think of Strix references in those books. That\u2019s a strange way to introduce metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T08:12:47-08:00","id":1350824,"title":"","content":"I think the Strix created the Julii, but I don't think they created all vampires. I think each clan has a different creation myth and their similarities are a result of convergent evolution (did I use that right?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T09:18:07-08:00","id":1352618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342587-diablerising-a-strix?p=1350824#post1350824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Strix created the Julii, but I don't think they created all vampires. I think each clan has a different creation myth and their similarities are a result of convergent evolution (did I use that right?).</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that the Requiem origin of the Clans, yes. Personally I kind of like a common creation for them but that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T09:53:14-08:00","id":1352628,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"970\" data-vbnamecard=\"970\">Gurkhal</a> what's your common creation theory for the clans in V:tR?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T07:52:56-08:00","id":1352811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342587-diablerising-a-strix?p=1352628#post1352628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"970\" data-vbnamecard=\"970\">Gurkhal</a> what's your common creation theory for the clans in V:tR?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did like many of those presented in the &quot;Mythologies&quot; supplement to 1st edition.<br /> <br /> My two favorites of my own ideas are:<br /> <br /> That the first vampires were the Nephilim who escaped destruction in the Flood, while the Strix are the spirits of the Nephilim who had their bodies destroyed<br /> <br /> Or that the first vampires were five children born to Lilith and that she used her magic to make them undead in order to cheat God's punishment that her children would die.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T09:23:09-08:00","id":1352825,"title":"","content":"I like the Lilith idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T09:50:56-08:00","id":1352827,"title":"","content":"I've never liked the idea of convergent evolution because there's no way all the Clans share all the base Kindred traits and even have their most obvious unique traits (in-Clan Disciplines) compatible with each other unless there's something tying them together. But disregarding convergent evolution doesn't mean all the Clans have to share a single origin. All Bloodlines of a Clan are related because they developed from that Clan, but all of them still developed independently from each other at different points in time and under different circumstances. I see no reason why something similar couldn't be the case for the Clans as well.<br /> At the very least there should be something that brought the Clans closer (be it an intelligence or a force) if the Clans truly do have separate origins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T10:54:31-08:00","id":1352833,"title":"","content":"The convergent evolution theory (from NH:WD) goes something like this. It initially seems weird that five totally unrelated and separate organisms would end up looking so similar. Except, the clans <i>aren't</i> entirely unrelated. They all have the same starting point: a human corpse. What if all the similarities actually result from the &quot;host&quot;, not from the &quot;parasite&quot; inside? Shared abilities like &quot;Resilience&quot; are actually vague groupings of many similar-looking ways to withstand pain, whether that involves psychologically shutting off that part of your mind, or physically strengthening your bones and muscles. A Mekhet who learns Resilience might be twisting their &quot;biology&quot; in a totally different way from a Gangrel who has it innately.<br /> <br /> Now, the thing this <i>doesn't</i> explain particularly well is the Beast, and in 2e, where all Disciplines are linked to the Beast, that's somewhat more of a problem. So if I were going to defend this IC, I'd have to modify it slightly: the clans started as five different ways of keeping a corpse &quot;alive&quot; through a steady diet of others' life-force, and those five were then &quot;infected&quot; with the Beast. (Strix involvement, maybe?) All five clans can learn Auspex because that's a trait of the Beast, but not all five clans get addicted to the people they feed on, because that was only a trait of the proto-Daeva, not of the proto-Ventrue or proto-Nosferatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T11:07:30-08:00","id":1352834,"title":"","content":"Question<br /> <br /> Is the Beast an actual thing or just like a metaphor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T11:15:27-08:00","id":1352838,"title":"","content":"We've gotten <i>way</i> off-topic, but\u2026<br /> <br /> Good question! Depends who you ask!<br /> <br /> There's <i>something</i> different between vampires and mortals. You can call it the Blood, you can call it the Curse, you can call it the Beast, but it definitely exists.<br /> <br /> Is there actually a separate entity that possesses you during frenzy? Up to the ST, but in my games, absolutely not. In my games, &quot;the Beast did it&quot; is the equivalent of &quot;the Devil made me do it&quot;: a way for vampires to feel better about the monstrous things they did. In other words, there's no nice clear dividing line between &quot;the Beast&quot; and &quot;the vampire as a whole&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T12:18:05-08:00","id":1352848,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24808_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24808\" data-vbnamecard=\"24808\">Draconis</a> thank you! We can get back on topic now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T06:08:53-08:00","id":1352993,"title":"","content":"My take on Convergent evolution:<br /> <br /> Evolution - implies there is a change over time, the end state is not the starting state.<br /> Convergence - It's not convergence if they start very similar and then don't get more similar as time goes by. That would be 'parallel' rather than convergent.<br /> <br /> In essence, when speaking of the convergent evolution theory, you could start with having 3 elements in-common:<br /> 1) Dead human<br /> 2) Drinks blood<br /> 3) Powerful blood that can change itself and others<br /> <br /> #3 wouldn't even be needed by all 5, one of the 5 could be enough.<br /> <br /> So you have these traits, but aside from that, the 5 are different. What happens when one feeds from one of the other types? Well, because of #3 and their inherent existing compatibility (#1&amp;#2), the powerful blood they drink may transform them in some ways, or their own blood may imitate it and lead to transformation in that way.<br /> <br /> After a few hundred years of these 5 types getting into contact with one another's blood, the pool of abilities has become more universal, with smaller differences.<br /> <br /> Sounds perfectly plausible to me. 'They just happen to have different versions of Resilience' does not work for me, and does't seem to align with the fact that you can learn a Resilience dot from diablerie of someone of another clan and the like... unless you're saying you're becoming more like that other clan through diablerie, in which case that's the above example again. ^^<br /> <br /> In such a view of vampiric origins, the Strix could have made one of the clans (Julii, then), or not. They could be a potential source for a 6th clan if you decide they're similar enough to vampires that 'convergent evolution' could take a next step with them. Personally I'd likely say they're too different, but that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T07:28:00-08:00","id":1353011,"title":"","content":"What you're describing works for me, being a take on the &quot;force&quot; I mentioned in my last post. It's not my preferred take, but I don't necessarily dislike it.<br /> However, convergent evolution refers to <i>independent</i> evolution to similar states, which is pretty different from what you described.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T09:14:34-08:00","id":1353370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342587-diablerising-a-strix?p=1353011#post1353011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you're describing works for me, being a take on the &quot;force&quot; I mentioned in my last post. It's not my preferred take, but I don't necessarily dislike it.<br /> However, convergent evolution refers to <i>independent</i> evolution to similar states, which is pretty different from what you described.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's so misleadingly named! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I suppose it still applies since they independently evolved the traits that then allow them to &quot;merge&quot;... some liberties must be taken when dealing with immortal monsters with magic blood, I suppose! xD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T10:49:50-08:00","id":1353385,"title":"","content":"Worth remembering that the way vampiric &quot;evolution&quot; works on an observable timeframe is a combination of line of descent and accumulating qualities from their prey and territory \u2014 vampires adapt to suit their feeding grounds and warp their feeding grounds to suit them in turn, and that happens in addition to whatever they pick up from their choice of prey.<br /> <br /> In other words, the Kindred are Kindred because they're made from people, feed on people, and mostly lair in places where people go. The Blood providing certain archetypal Disciplines could well be a function of those qualities being particularly prominent in the parts of the world vampirism partakes of and untouched spontaneous Embraces being particularly uncommon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T18:21:53-08:00","id":1354020,"title":"","content":"Have to disagree completely with <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro\">Illuminostro</a></b>. What I love about Requiem is city-building / NPC building / story building - you are given a lot of tools if you like, but you can also completely do your own thing too and there is no &quot;meta&quot; really in that way (though there are few stereotypes if you want - but no more Vykos or Beckett or Theo Bell or whoever their names are). The Strix are never given a definite origin or purpose or anything - your chronicle can completely skip them, give them any role you want, or be a complete counterpoint to a vampire's humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T19:06:12-08:00","id":1354278,"title":"","content":"How would you even diablerize a Strix is a Strix can't fall into torpor? Correct me if I'm wrong, but if I remember correctly: when the Strix is possessing a vampire, human or corpse, it gets kicked out of the body the moment the host dies. That means, the moment you actually get the opportunity to attempt diablerie on the Strix, the Strix is already out of the body. And how would one diablerize a floating shadowy smokey owl?<br /> <br /> If what I say is incorrect, then I know this to be correct for certain: a Strix can simply eject itself out of the body at any time, taking a turn to do so. So any Strix with half a brain would leave its host behind the moment that host is close to dying.<br /> <br /> So yeah, either diablerizing a Strix is utterly impossible, or as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a> said, it should be near impossible and an extremely rare occurance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T19:50:18-08:00","id":1354282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342587-diablerising-a-strix?p=1350824#post1350824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Strix created the Julii, but I don't think they created all vampires. I think each clan has a different creation myth and their similarities are a result of convergent evolution (did I use that right?).</div> </div> </div> </div>While it isn't confirmed, it's heavily suggested that <i>all</i> vampire clans are the creation of the Strix. Vampires existed before the Strix, but it's the Strix that gave the vampires clans and with it, their Beast, and thus the vampires became Kindred. It's why the &quot;convergent evolution&quot; happened, I think.<br /> <br /> The evidence? Well, like I said, there is no hard evidence, but there is plenty of lore to back up this hypothesis. The first clue is in the description of the Strix going by the name of 'Mother', in the Vampire: the Requiem, Second Edition Core Rulebook.<br /> <br /> Another less obvious and less convincing piece of evidence is in the Synthesis Dread Power the Strix gain, which allows them to create new Kindred (but not new clans, so that's why I think this point isn't a very convincing one).<br /> <br /> A third clue can be found in Night Horrors - The Wicked Dead, where there is a story of a clanless group of vampires being granted a clan by the Strix. This gift made the vampires better predators, but it also gave them the Beast. This story hints at the Julii, but at the same time also contradicts the Julii's origin story (where Remus bargains with the Strix as he lay dying, and then rose up as the first Julii). At any rate, this story does seem to suggest that Strix can give clanless vampires a clan. If that's the case, then could perhaps all Kindred clans be created this way?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T03:36:40-08:00","id":1354330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tomorrow's Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342587-diablerising-a-strix?p=1354278#post1354278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you even diablerize a Strix is a Strix can't fall into torpor? Correct me if I'm wrong, but if I remember correctly: when the Strix is possessing a vampire, human or corpse, it gets kicked out of the body the moment the host dies.</div> </div> </div> </div>When attempting diablerie, the victim doesn't die at full aggravated until the diablerie is completed or broken off. (And, if using a Scale in Secrets of the Covenants, <i>you can survive even that!</i>)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tomorrow's Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342587-diablerising-a-strix?p=1354282#post1354282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it isn't confirmed, it's heavily suggested that <i>all</i> vampire clans are the creation of the Strix. Vampires existed before the Strix, but it's the Strix that gave the vampires clans and with it, their Beast, and thus the vampires became Kindred. It's why the &quot;convergent evolution&quot; happened, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>The description for &quot;Mother&quot; does bring up the possibility of Strix creating Clans other than Julii, but Julii are definitely singled out among them. Other than that I don't think your examples heavily suggest anything. If the Strix created one Clan, then maybe they <i>can</i> create more? Possibly. Even probably, imo. But it doesn't suggest that the Strix necessarily <i>did</i> create any other Clans.<br /> <br /> As for the discrepancy in the Julii origin story, remember that Romulus and Remus are purely apocryphal characters first mentioned 500 years after their supposed existence, and that it is Remus' supposed childe Julius Senex who's credited with any historical accomplishments in the Necropolis as well as giving name to the Clan. Treat what's said in Requiem for Rome as the Julii version of the story passed down through generations, altered or even made up completely to fit the narrative of the Julii, and what's written in Wicked Dead as the Strix version of the story, altered or even made up completely to fit the narrative of the owls.<br /> <br /> Additionally, there has always been hints towards Gangrels and Ventrue sharing some ancestry. Since the Ventrue almost certainly came from the Julii in first edition, the Julii might've originally been Gangrel who changed Clan/had their Clan changed, quite possibly due to the Strix. If so, the Strix hasn't showed any ability to create a new Clan from scratch, only modifying an existing Clan.<br /> In second edition it's less likely that the Ventrue are descendants from Julii, or, if they are, that the Julii are related to the Gangrel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T05:37:08-08:00","id":1354339,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25286_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25286\" data-vbnamecard=\"25286\">Tomorrow's Nobody</a> hmmm. Interesting. I'm gonna have to think about this. Your idea does sound tempting...<br /> <br /> But counter-argument: what about the First Edition clanbooks that give a different origin story for every clan (except the Ventrue)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T15:31:44-08:00","id":1354682,"title":"","content":"Myths and also, it's first edition","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T11:42:40-08:00","id":1354798,"title":"","content":"The 2e corebook also provides different origin myths for all the clans; I see no issue adding the 1e clanbook myths to that set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T22:45:09-08:00","id":1354963,"title":"","content":"What you say makes a lot of sense, Tessie. I do have my own theories on the following though:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342587-diablerising-a-strix?p=1354330#post1354330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, there has always been hints towards Gangrels and Ventrue sharing some ancestry. Since the Ventrue almost certainly came from the Julii in first edition, the Julii might've originally been Gangrel who changed Clan/had their Clan changed, quite possibly due to the Strix. If so, the Strix hasn't showed any ability to create a new Clan from scratch, only modifying an existing Clan.<br /> In second edition it's less likely that the Ventrue are descendants from Julii, or, if they are, that the Julii are related to the Gangrel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Julii and Gangrel are related, but:<br /> <br /> I think the Ventrue are the result of rampant diablerie. The Gangrel diablerizing the Julii, or the Julii diablerizing Gangrel, until at some point the resulting vampire wasn't just a new bloodline, but an entirely new clan. Perhaps a Julii coterie manages to change their clan through diablerie in order to avoid the Strix, thus the Ventrue were born. Maybe some opportunistic Gangrel took full use of the fall of the Camarilla and went on a mission to steal the Julii's clan power, resulting in the Ventrue clan. Maybe a Julii spawned a Revenant who got uplifted by a Gangrel, but instead of the Revenant becoming another Gangrel, he became the first Ventrue. Or maybe, just maybe, the Strix saw fit to give the Julii's Dominate power to a very loyal Gangrel who helped them destroy clan Julii (Victrix?) and this became the start of a new clan: clan Ventrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T05:29:27-08:00","id":1354984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tomorrow's Nobody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342587-diablerising-a-strix?p=1354963#post1354963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the Julii and Gangrel are related</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, in first edition. The <i>only</i> difference between Julii and Ventrue was whether they got a penalty on <i>detachment</i> or <i>derangement</i> checks. Anything common to both Gangrel and Ventrue would also be common to Gangrel and Julii, making it highly probable that whatever ties there are between the former dated back to the creation of the Founders.<br /> (And one might also argue that both Gangrel and Julii lose their humanity, by becoming more animalistic and beastly, respectively, where the Ventrue instead lose their sanity, making Ventrue diverge further <i>away</i> from Gangrel rather than towards them.)<br /> <br /> In second edition, it's a lot less likely because of the different Clan Banes and Discipline spreads. (Notably, Julii got Dominate, Resilience and <i>Vigor</i>.) The Julii's transformation into the Ventrue (if you subscribe to that idea) put them noticeably closer to the Gangrel (Disciplines lined up more, the Clan Banes being closer in themes), suggesting that any ties between Gangrel and Ventrue dates back to the latter's creation rather than to the Julii.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T13:25:16-08:00","id":1364397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342587-diablerising-a-strix?p=1354984#post1354984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I said, in first edition. The <i>only</i> difference between Julii and Ventrue was whether they got a penalty on <i>detachment</i> or <i>derangement</i> checks. Anything common to both Gangrel and Ventrue would also be common to Gangrel and Julii, making it highly probable that whatever ties there are between the former dated back to the creation of the Founders.<br /> (And one might also argue that both Gangrel and Julii lose their humanity, by becoming more animalistic and beastly, respectively, where the Ventrue instead lose their sanity, making Ventrue diverge further <i>away</i> from Gangrel rather than towards them.)<br /> <br /> In second edition, it's a lot less likely because of the different Clan Banes and Discipline spreads. (Notably, Julii got Dominate, Resilience and <i>Vigor</i>.) The Julii's transformation into the Ventrue (if you subscribe to that idea) put them noticeably closer to the Gangrel (Disciplines lined up more, the Clan Banes being closer in themes), suggesting that any ties between Gangrel and Ventrue dates back to the latter's creation rather than to the Julii.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fair analysis.<br /> <br /> My personal fan theory is that the Ventrue are the result of rampant diablerie among the Julii. Maybe the Ventrue started as a Julii bloodline with Animalism. However, a friend of mine agrees with you and proposed an alternative: the Ventrue being the result of a Gangrel diablerizing Julii. Maybe the Ventrue started as a Gangrel bloodline with Dominate. Wouldn't that be something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25286-tomorrow-s-nobody","name":"Tomorrow's Nobody","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}